From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:14:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feature: turn off feedback and analytics by default and point
 the update check at our releases

This client must not send feedback or product analytics to OpenAI unless the user opts in, and its update
check must not offer OpenAI's npm, bun, pnpm, Vite+ or Homebrew packages, which would replace this build with
upstream's.

Feedback and analytics already have upstream switches that every sender honours, so the patch changes the
switches' defaults instead of adding gates. `feedback.enabled` and an unset `analytics.enabled` now resolve to
false when the configuration loads, and `/feedback` is neither listed nor resolved because the command list
cannot read the configuration. The built-in Statsig exporter follows `analytics.enabled`, so it sends nothing
unless the user turns analytics on.

The update check queries holdmyspot-com/codex-unleashed releases, and the installer commands and release links
name that repository. Package-manager installs get no upgrade action. Release tags look like
`rust-v0.167.0+<build>`, so the version comparison reads the numeric build after `+`; with no build it is 0.

Tests that rely on the old defaults now enable feedback or analytics explicitly.
